From 8bf2c70657bc8191cf88fa6a92aea357889699d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cucumberfeet <116314769+cucumberfeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:07:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: prevent System blip for mapped apps (pulse/WP rules)

When pipewire-pulse stamps node.target=<default sink>, WirePlumber skips
stream-properties restore and briefly links the app to System. Generate
pulse.rules + a WirePlumber linking override from the profile so
target.object points at the mapped pipeweaver_* channel on first connect.
Also skip the 250ms ApplicationAdded discovery wait when the app already
has a profile mapping.

